\section{URL enumeration}{

The list endpoint is
\verb{GET /umbraco/api/license/getall?caseType=00&county=00&filterText=&municipality=00&pageNumber=N}
(JSON). Its \code{Licenses} array carries the case records; \code{Counties},
\code{Municipalities}, \code{CaseTypes}, and \code{LicenseStatuses} are filter-vocab facets
returned inline, and \code{TotalCount} is the unfiltered count. The defaults
\verb{caseType=00&county=00&municipality=00&filterText=} mean "all". The page
generator (\code{no_fetch_search()}) paginates \verb{pageNumber = 1, 2, …} until a page
returns no \code{Licenses} (parsed with \code{perform_json}). The canonical detail URL
for each record is the human page
\verb{https://www.nve.no/konsesjon/konsesjonssaker/konsesjonssak?id=\{SoknadId\}&type=\{Type\}}.
}

\section{Attachments}{

Each detail page renders the case documents in one or more \code{div.n-filelist}
sections, each with an \verb{<h2>} section heading (e.g. \emph{Konsesjon}) and a list
of \verb{<a>} links to downloadable PDFs at
\verb{https://webfileservice.nve.no/API/PublishedFiles/Download/<saksnummer>/<fileId>}
(and a UUID variant \verb{.../Download/<uuid>/<saksnummer>/<fileId>}); no
authentication is needed. The handler scrapes those links (sidecar-first),
grouping the URLs by the section heading into per-section
\verb{attachment_urls_<slug>} columns (the DE / IT / SK pattern; the slug is the
ASCII-folded Norwegian heading) plus the deduplicated union in
\code{attachment_urls}. EIA documents are \strong{not} type-flagged in the markup, so
every case document is collected; the document label/title is kept verbatim
(in the link's \verb{<h3>}) so downstream can identify
"konsekvensutredning" / "KU" / "melding" by filename. A case with no
published files yields an empty \code{attachment_urls} vector, which is valid.
}

